Jeff Dykzeul wrote:
> I think the "last" command will be adequate for my reporting needs, but I
> also need to be able to clear out the wtmp file. I can't find or am
> overlooking the command or script to do this. In VMS typically you would
> close the accounting database, rename it to some archival name, and then
> start a new one. Basically I want to do the same thing in dUnix. Anybody
> have any suggestions?

man wtmp gives a rather indirect hint.

  The wtmp file is maintained by login(1) and init(8).  Neither of these pro-
  grams creates the file, so, if it is removed, record keeping is turned off.

So:
	# mv /var/adm/wtmp <archival name>
	# touch /var/adm/wtmp
