>
>Greetings
>	I am looking for a way to limit an interactive login session
>	for say 1000s of CPU time. Basically, I would like everyone
>	whose jobs take more than 1000s CPU time to run in batch mode.
>	The current batch environment is Crays NQE.
>	How do I limit "non-root" process interactive limit? 
>	I am running the Digital UNIX version 4.0
>	Thanks in Advance
>	cheers
>	Mohan

You want to use the ulimit command in /etc/profile and the limit command in the
C-shell startup file (probably /etc/csh.login). See the man pages for sh, ksh,
bash, csh, tcsh ...

On OSF 3.2 the Bourne shell only lets you set soft limits, not hard limits. I
don't know whether this is still true in DUnix 4.0.

Bob
