In article <4t20eq$cgf@seagoon.newcastle.edu.au>,
Tony Dyson <tony@linus.newcastle.edu.au> wrote:
> Has anyone modified the CDE behaviour to change the default
> terminal to something besides dtterm? (eg xterm?)
> 
> I've read the documentation and tried all kinds of things to no
> avail.

In your $HOME/.dt/types directory, create a file that ends with a  .dt
suffix.  In that file, put:

ACTION Terminal
{
        TYPE            MAP
        MAP_ACTION      Xterm
}


Log out and log back in, and you should have xterm as your terminal from
then on.

All the above action does is change the mapping so that when the `Terminal'
action is run (try `dtaction Terminal' from the command line), instead of
the default mapping of running the `Dtterm' action, it runs the Xterm action,
which is defined in one of the files in /usr/dt/appconfig/types/C.

Tim
