Jeff Katcher wrote:
> 
> I just upgraded my AlphaStation 200 4/166's firmware using the AS200_v5_6.EXE
> file on the appropriate Digital server.  The upgrade seemed to go successfully
> except when I verified the upgrade, a verify error was reported for
> ARC/AlphaBIOS.  Is this a problem?  DU3.2 runs fine, but any error makes me
> nervous.
> 
> Thanks in advance for any help/advice...
> 
> Jeffrey Katcher
> EMail: katcher@netcom.COM

Jeff,

The AlphaStation 200 systems originally had 1 MB of flashROM - enough to hold the ARC
firmware for the Windows NT o/s and the SRM firmware for the OpenVMS and Digital UNIX o/s. 
Later half of the flashROM was removed. This meant either ARC or SRM could be loaded, but 
not both. Typing "verify" at the APU prompt tried to verify both, even though you have 
only SRM, hence the error. Try typing "verify srm" to check just the SRM firmware image.

--Terry 
