>OSF/1 claims it has realtime features. What is the correct procedure to 
>configure the kernel to have these features? 

They're enabled by default in DU4.0. Use doconfig to enable it in previous
versions. With 4.0, you can set rt-preemt-opt=1 (in /etc/sysconfigtab,
generic options, see sysconfigtab man page).

