> : storage works rack and an external scsi port.  According to the
> : documentation if I use the internal storage works rack I can't use the
> : external port.  Since it has a CD-ROM drive installed I am left with
> : only 6 slots for my 8 storage works drives.  I was also hoping to
> : connect our TZ867 tape drive to the back of it.
> 
> I noticed an external SCSI interface at the back of 2100 5/250.
> I thought that that interface could be used for connecting
> a tape drive.  Am I wrong?  Will using that interface disable
> the internal SCSI?  Someone please confirm this. In case
> a second controller is needed, what are the popular ones?
> Going to a Raid?   We just bought a TZ88N tape drive and
> I haven't tried to connect it yet.  I am panic with this
> new information.
> 

I initially made this mistake with our 2100s. I simply plugged a DAT drive
into the external bus at the back. Worked fine until (bizarrely) I upgraded
the Alpha firmware and suddenly my SCSI bus kept resetting and trashing
the disks. Basically if you've got an internal Storage Works rack you can't
use the external SCSI port because that takes you over the 3 meter limit.
My solution was to backup remotely instead... If you've got the money just
stick another PCI SCSI card in and move the external cable to this card.

Mark
