Tony Dyson wrote:
> 
> Has anyone modified the CDE behaviour to change the default
> terminal to something besides dtterm? (eg xterm?)
> 

You should be able to edit the file /usr/dt/appconfig/types/C/dt.dt and
change the EXEC_STRING for the ACTION Dtterm from /usr/dt/bin/dtterm -ls
to /usr/bin/X11/xterm. You'll get xterm instead of dtterm when clicking
on the terminal icon.

If you only want to do it for one user, rather than systemwide, copy
dt.dt to $HOME/.dt/types, then edit it to include just the Dtterm
ACTION, and change dtterm to xterm in the EXEC_STRING.



