From: "R.Whittington" <r.whittington@dl.ac.uk>
Subject: OPEN3D/ZLXp support within V4.0 oops!
Date: 1996/07/17
Message-ID: <31EC2E6E.41C6@dl.ac.uk>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 168554143
cc: tris <t.a.p.green@dl.ac.uk>, m.enderby@dl.ac.uk
content-type: text/plain; charset=us-ascii
organization: Daresbury Lab, Warrington, U.K.
mime-version: 1.0
newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1
x-mailer: Mozilla 3.0b4 (X11; I; OSF1 V3.2 alpha)


I've just spent a day and a half tracking down a "hardware
fault" with engineer in attendance. Whilst the thing
(Alpha 255/233 with ZLXp2-EV4) reported Machine Check 0x660
it turns out that the ZLXp is an unsupported option until OPEN3D v4.0

Strange I should be able to buy such hardware before the
software to support it is shipping!

I first saw the problem the first reboot after i completed the OSF/1
V3.2D FIS customisation. Boot OSF blah blah, then just on the
controller tga0 config line, whoops over it went. I rebooted
again and it came up OK.

I managed for a few weeks just rebooting with patience and then
i upgraded to v4.0. Well, it hardened the fault, as they say.

Panic (cpu 0) hardware error - machine check 0x660

a hardware error you'd think? so did i, so i called DEC. After
the day and half we'd replaced the motherboard, graphics board,
re-installed V4.0, re-installed firmware and still the machine
check was there!!! (we thought the fault must be in the CD volume
control at this point).

After all this, the techie back at base found some internal DEC
article which said that OSF/1 v4.0 requires OPEN3D v4.0 which
doesn't ship until "late July". But, of course, the ZLXp card
requires OPEN3D to work. I believe, since I saw the errors with
v3.2, that the prolem exists there too.

can anyone confirm this analysis? what's the line on this?
it couldn't be a screw-up could it?

cheers,
royd.

BTW, throughout the engineer showed persistence and skill. And
I am left with a system which usually boots with v3.2 and
an explanation, of sorts - thanks.

