>Please help!
>I'm trying to compile mush 6.4 under OSF/1 on DEC Alpha, and I'm having
>no luck at all. I previously compiled it under Ultrix just using BSD
>makefile, but under OSF I cannot compile it at all - the first file
>to compile gives fatal errors. I didn't want to attach the printout - it
>would be too long posting, but if someone can help me, I could e-mail
>it, of course.
>Thanks,
>Fedor Pikus

mush makes a lot of assumptions about integer sizes and such (for example,
UNIX stores the time in four bytes, which is a "long" on most systems but is
an "int" on OSF/1; the author used "long" instead of "time_t", so there's
a lot of search-and-replace that needs doing), which make it very hard to port
to OSF/1.  I have v7.2.6 compiled on the Alpha, but it still randomly
coredumps sometimes while you're in the editor composing a message.  I haven't
yet figured out what code segment causes this, and haven't had time to work
on it a whole lot lately.
