John Allen - GeoNet (johna@ATCON.COM) wrote:

Hi John,

: 
: I would also like to back up data residing on drives on various TCP/IP
: networked pc's running SCO Unix, Windows 3.11, and Windows '95.  =
: 
: 
: Anybody know of any off-theshelf products or shareware utilities which
: will  do this?  Must I first get the drives mounted NFS?
: 

Backing up the file systems should not be a problem.  The difficult part 
is planning to restore the data.

If you can NFS mount the drives onto the Alpha, you should be able to backup
and restore data files without problem.  (Operating system backups need to be 
restored from a local device - no networking available)

FWIW, Digital UNIX V4.0 contains a single-server version of Networker backup
software.  This will enable you to backup and restore local file systems on
the Alpha.  The full version can be licenced from DEC (or Legato).  This will
enable you to remotely backup or restore data files on PC's and UNIX systems
and manage the tapes for you.

There are probably a number of freeware or shareware remote archive 
programs available for PC's, and UNIX data files can be backed up and 
restored via rdump.

I hope this helps.  Let me know if you have any questions

All the best
Allan



