>Rock Ridge Interchange Protocol. Apparently this is not so.   I just 
>recently had to use the "noversion" option when mounting a cd to view it 
>properly.  The "rrip" obviously was not the correct option.
>What is the proper way to tell which option to choose (aside from trial 
>and error)? 

ISO 9660 specifies 8+3+version, so that's what's "proper".  By mounting the
CD "noversion" you make the version numbers invisible, which is apparently
what you wanted, giving you just 8+3, which is nonstandard but much easier
to use.

RRIP extends ISO 9660 by adding UNIX-like file naming: long names, mixed
case, arbitrarily deep directory trees.  It's useless unless the CD is made
with RRIP, and I'd guess yours wasn't.

