You can also do this with LSM, which is the LVM replacement.  You
might want to consider migrating because LVM will probably go away
someday (but not in V4.0).

>If this volume contains already a UFS, can I increase
>the UFS size as well? This is in dUnix 3.2C.

Nope.  For reasons I don't fully understand, we elected to take
out the utility that the Open Software Foundation provided to
do this.  On older systems you can find the manual page for it,
but no command.  Pity.  AdvFS doesn't recognize "new" space
either, but at least it supports adding new volumes.

