>	It really looks awful to have the X window with resolution
>1024x768. Especially I just could not figure out why there are two
>different resolutions with the same graphics adapters and monitors?

Sounds like the frequency setting jumper pins may be set incorrectly.
We have several PMAGB-BC boards set for 60 Hz which generates 1024x864
pixels.  The boards show up on the system as "PMAGB-BA", so perhaps
you have one of these variant boards, either a -BC or -BE.  Check whether
there is a jumper on the oscillator setting pins and try removing and see 
what happens.

