> 
> As an added bonus (in 4.0), most of the buggy
> GUI sysadmin tools won't work without CDE installed.

Which ones would those be? The sysadmin tools work properly on a
standard X display, using twm, mwm, etc. as a window manager. There is
no dependency on the CDE desktop nor the CDE window or session managers.
That was always a design criteria. In fact, if you use DecWindows
instead of CDE (an option at configuration time), the sysadmin tools
show up in the application set.

