this code should, on our version of the compiler (V5.1), cause a run time
floating exception (for divide by zero). Instead, the division becomes zero.


My long term goal, of course, is to test it with the V5.3 compiler (which
is supposed to support the IEEE float standards) using the flag 
-ieee_with_no_inexact,
to see if I can get the IEEE standard result (which would be, literally, 
infinity). But since the division goes thru DIGITALS C++ complex library,
I question if this will work correctly.

If anyone can do the test on the V5.3 compiler and let me know the results 
(and DIGITAL, if there is still a bug) I would appreciate it. I am trying to 
get the support people here to upgrade to the latest and greatest compiler,
and swat this problem down for good.


here is my missbehaving code

----------------------------------------------------------------------------

