Bryan Lally (lally@lanl.gov) wrote:
: A little help, please ...

: I just installed a FDDI adaptor (DEFTA-AA) in an AXP 3000/400, running
: dUnix 3.2D.  I seem to need some software to make it work.  Anyone know
: what I need to install, and which disk I'll find it on?

: MAKEDEV doesn't seem to know how to make /dev/fta0, which is what I need to see.

You need to add a line:

controller      fta0       at tc0       slot ? vector    ftaintr

to your kernel configuration file, rebuild/install the kernel, and
reboot. 

Network devices don't show up in /dev; use "netstat -ni" to see them,
ifconfig to configure them.

Stephen
