I have two network interfaces, ether (ln0) and FDDI (fta0).  I just got
the FDDI interface, and I have a small problem.  Perhaps it's already been
solved?

I would like everything to use the FDDI interface, if possible.  However,
I need to run CAP (Columbia Appletalk Package) on this machine, to provide
network printing service.  CAP doesn't seem to be able to deal with the
FDDI interface, and can't get an appletalk node number.  Unless I turn on
the ether interface, and run CAP out that spigot.  A fix for CAP on fta0
would solve the problem.  This problem seems to be related to the fact
that pfstat reports pf/pfilt1 being connected to the FDDI interface, and
